// Phase 5 5D-9: bindingness of a voucher — separates real transactions from
// non-binding paper documents. REGULAR posts GL / moves stock (sale, purchase,
// payment, receipt, journal…); OPTIONAL is a non-binding document with no GL
// and no stock impact (estimate, order, quote) whose status is a free document
// lifecycle. Replaces scattered hardcoded type-lists (e.g. the status-toggle
// route's TOGGLEABLE set) — `type` stays purely descriptive, this carries
// behaviour. Derived from `type` at spine creation via bindingForType()
// (src/shared/lib/accountancy/voucherBinding.ts).
enum VoucherBinding {
  REGULAR
  OPTIONAL
}

