// ── Pricing-strategy enums ────────────────────────────────────────────────────

// Cost-basis method used by the pricing-strategy resolver and the BS valuation
// dropdown. Selected per InvProduct (override) or org-wide via
// OrgDefaults.valuationMethod. Each method derives the unit cost in paise as:
//   WEIGHTED_AVG  → Σ(qty × rate) / Σ(qty) over every inward lot
//                   (opening lot + all POSTED inward ledger rows). Default.
//   SIMPLE_AVG    → Σ(rate) / N — plain arithmetic mean, qty doesn't weight.
//                   Use when batch size shouldn't influence the cost basis.
//   FIFO          → walk lots newest-first against current on-hand qty.
//   LAST_INWARD   → most recent inward lot's rate (any inward type:
//                   PURCHASE / GRN / SALE_RETURN / MJ-PRODUCE / PHYSICAL_STOCK).
//   MONTHLY_AVG   → weighted avg restricted to the current calendar month;
//                   fallback to LAST_INWARD when no purchases this month.
// Cascading fallback for every method when there's no usable history:
//   method-empty → LAST_INWARD → openingRate → no-cost-basis (Needs Attention).
//
// Renamed from LAST_PURCHASE_COST → LAST_INWARD in PR 3 of noble-boole.
// STD_COST + LIFO dropped (STD was dead weight; LIFO banned for Indian tax).
enum CostMethod {
  WEIGHTED_AVG
  SIMPLE_AVG
  FIFO
  LAST_INWARD
  MONTHLY_AVG
}

// PricingScope removed 2026-05-26 — PricingStrategy now uses multi-condition
// matching (brandIds[], groupIds[], categoryIds[], attrFilters, cost/stock/
// staleness ranges) instead of a single scope dimension. See
// prisma/schema/inventory.prisma#PricingStrategy.

// Dimensions of the additive-margin "strategy points" model (StrategyPoint).
// A product's margin% is the SUM of the points of the dimension values it
// falls under. BASE is the single org-wide baseline; BRAND/CATEGORY/GROUP key
// on a master id; the *_BAND values key on a fixed band key (stock level /
// idle age / movement). See prisma/schema/inventory.prisma#StrategyPoint.
enum StrategyPointDimension {
  BASE
  BRAND
  CATEGORY
  GROUP
  PRODUCT
  STOCK_BAND
  AGE_BAND
  MOVE_BAND
}

// Which source materializes a product's effectiveSalePricePaise (the price every
// sale transaction charges). Chosen on Update & Print Labels / Edit Product.
//   STRATEGY  — the live PricingStrategy engine output.
//   COMPUTED  — live cost × the product's own marginPercent.
//   SAVED     — the human-frozen savedSalePricePaise (also the barcode source).
// The recompute trigger writes the chosen source into InvProduct.effectiveSalePricePaise.
enum EffectiveSalePriceSource {
  STRATEGY
  COMPUTED
  SAVED
}

// Kind of an AdditionalCostAllocation row — how a slice of a shipping/courier
// pool entry is consumed.
//   ALLOCATION — attributed to a product as a per-unit additional cost (pricing only).
//   DISMISSAL  — written off as general office/courier expense, leaves the waiting list.
// Decision-support only — neither kind posts to the GL.
enum AdditionalCostAllocationKind {
  ALLOCATION
  DISMISSAL
}

